# Profile: all-on - The default profile: every feature flag on, except the live-messaging, closed-loop and alert sends that need an owner's approval.
# Generated by npm run flags:docs from src/lib/flags/profiles.ts. Do not edit by hand: change the profile and regenerate.
# Names and safe values only. A flag is on only for the exact value 1. NEXT_PUBLIC_* names are set at BUILD time (a change needs a rebuild).
# Every feature flag on, with consent enforcement. Live messaging (CleverTap writes, the nudger), closed-loop conversions, Google Chat lead alerts and the RM daily brief email (it sends to real RMs) are commented out in the template: each needs the owner's approval before it is switched on. Closed-loop has no per-send approval in code, so turning it on is the approval. Off on purpose: demo mode, the closed-loop fake destination, sample partner data, SSO_ONLY and the blocked Autopilot apply switch. Defaults never supply credentials: AI keys, CRON_SECRET, ENCRYPTION_KEY and the rest must be set by the host. The CleverTap push path (src/lib/integrations/clevertap/push-batch.ts) sends only a batch an Admin requested and a different Admin approved (CLEVERTAP_PUSH_BATCH), exactly once, and an approved batch expires after 24 hours. With no approved batch it sends nothing.

